  "text": "**Neither solution is correct.** I checked the case d = 5 directly, since a formula's value there can rule it out.\n\n- For d = 5, the projection C_q lies in P³ and is a smooth genus-1 curve of degree 5.\n- A smooth genus-1 curve of degree 5 cannot lie on a quadric. On a smooth quadric it would be of bidegree (a,b) with a+b = 5 and (a−1)(b−1) = 1, which has no integer solutions. On a quadric cone, a smooth curve would need to be a complete intersection of the cone with a cubic, which has genus 4 and is not genus 1.\n- So h⁰(I_{C_q}(2)) = 0, and the ideal is not generated by quadrics. Property N₁ fails, so the Green–Lazarsfeld index is 0 at d = 5.\n\nChecking the candidates at d = 5:\n\n- **Solution 1** claims d − 3 = 2. This is wrong. It assumes the projection keeps the embedding of the original curve, but C_q is embedded in P^{d−2} by a codimension-1 subspace of H⁰(L), so the index of C itself does not transfer.\n- **Solution 2** claims d − 4 = 1. This is also wrong. Its N_p analysis is only a sketch, and it implicitly claims N₁ holds at d = 5, which the quadric check rules out.\n\nThe d = 5 check does not pin down the general formula, so I have not established the correct function of d. The only conclusion I can support is that neither proposed answer matches the index at d = 5.\n\nCHOICE: NONE",
